  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The verbal report contains no mention of probability distribution, favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes, or skewness. The individual's justification is based on a subjective emotional evaluation ('happy to be'), not on a comparison of distributional features. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason that evaluates skewness. The absence of any reference to distributional shape or probability weighting on favorable outcomes confirms that the reason was not applied.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
